police have launched a concerted effort  to tackle off-road motorcycle riders and  other nuisance behavior in woodland and  open spaces around the rochford district  local offices supported by a special  mountain bike squad and officers and  horses from the mounted section will  patrol woods country parks and private  farmland in a crackdown on anti-social  behavior  they will carry out stop checks on  motorcycles and quad bikes being ridden  illegally and will have the power to  seize vehicles from persistent offenders  the operation will be focused on new  england woods hockley woods gusted  hallwoods cherry orchard country park  edwards hall park fleming's farm and  grove woods  sergeant steve joins from the hockley  neighborhood policing team said the  irresponsible behaviour of the nuisance  motorcyclist is endangering horse riders  dog walkers and others using the woods  legitimately  they will often spend several hours  riding off-road and are literally riding  roughshod over other residents enjoyment  of the environment  we will deal robustly with anyone  behaving in such an anti-social manner  and i would ask anyone who sees bikers  riding in the woods or vehicles  offloading bikes to take a note of their  index number or any other details and  call us  police also have evidence of vandals  deliberately starting fires in woods and  fields and causing explosions by burning  aerosol cans further endangering  legitimate uses and putting unnecessary  strain on hard-pressed emergency  services  sergeant joyne said their foolish  behavior not only jeopardizes their own  safety and that of other people but also  represents a real threat to the woods  themselves  we are determined to stamp out this  nuisance and the availability of our  cycling squad allows us greater  accessibility over rough terrain it's  harder for people to get away from us  now  help keep your area safe with seven and  a half million members nationally  neighborhood watch plays a key role in  helping reduce opportunities for crime  and anti-social behavior it works to  improve community safety and reduce or  prevent crime by developing close  liaison between households and the  police and by promoting crime prevention  and home security advice  though not run by the police  neighborhood watch works in partnership  with them by letting police know of  anything suspicious in their area  members can help deter would-be burglars  and vandals  neighbourhood watch is also about  building communities spirit and good  relations among residents and is a  popular way for people of all ages to  get involved in making their area safe  membership of a neighborhood watch  scheme has other benefits too members  not only learn more about crime  prevention and home security to help  keep their property and possessions safe  but as a result may also qualify for a  discount on their house insurance  the rochford district neighborhood watch  team is looking to recruit keen  volunteers to become neighborhood watch  coordinators  if you would like details about setting  up a scheme please email nhw rayleigh at  essex dot pnn dot police dot uk  or contact mike hooper chairman of  rochefort district nhw on  zero one two six eight double seven zero  five one nine or care of the  neighborhood watch off israeli police  station 119 high street raleigh ss6 7qb  you can also take a look at the rochford  district neighborhood watch website to  find out more details about the scheme  the website address is www dot r r n w  dot c o m e z e dot com  neighborhood watch in association with  rochefort district community safety  partnership has extended its successful  and free bike security tagging campaign  program to local schools  mike hooper chairman of the neighborhood  watch and clive mayhew essex watch  coordinator for the rochford district  recently visited king edmund school with  deputy head sue nickel where more than  20 pupils took the opportunity to have  the security devices fitted to their  bikes  neighborhood watch by numbers  the rochford district neighborhood watch  team currently has 180 watch  coordinators covering 4451  properties across the rochford district  they also issue a newsletter once every  three months  the rochford district community safety  partnership the csp has pitched in to  help provide a soccer skills course for  young people in wakering  they have contributed 1  920 pound for a qualified coach to leave  twice weekly soccer sessions for  teenagers in a six-month pilot scheme  organised by the wakering young people's  community project  some 40 young people regularly attend  the project's team cafe twice a week  where football is among activities  available  the chair of the project's trustees  hillary wilson said the young people and  not only the boys have frequently  requested a coach to help them improve  their skills and to show them ways to  keep fit  this pilot scheme will give us an  opportunity to decide if a coach should  be engaged permanently and we're  grateful for the support of the csb in  helping fund this  vice chair of the csp chief inspector  glenn wesley said the teen cafe provides  a safe place for young people to enjoy  themselves and make new friends  it offers the diversionary activities  that young people enjoy and are  enthusiastic about like football and  which encourage a positive attitude and  social responsibility  we are wholeheartedly behind initiatives  like this  and the csp has recently received a  number of complaints about intrusive  telephone calls from sales companies  attempting to sell anything from loft  insulation to fitted kitchens  residents can do something to deter this  cold calling by registering their  telephone number with the telephone  preference service that's the tps  the tps maintains a central opt-out  register of people who do not wish to  receive  unsolicited sales or marketing telephone  calls  it is a legal requirement that companies  do not make such calls to numbers  registered with the tps  the service is free and once the number  has been registered it becomes effective  in 28 days  and to register call the tps  registration line on 0845  070707  or go to www.tpsonline.org.uk  and if you're receiving sales and  marketing voice recorded messages and  you have not given prior consent to  receive such messages you can ask the  marketeer to stop sending these  they are legally obliged to act upon  your request  however if you still receive calls or it  is not possible to ask the company to  stop sending these types of messages  contact the information commissioner's  office the ico  the government body responsible for  enforcing the regulations  for more information visit w w w dot  dot uk  or phone their helpline on zero one six  two five  five four five  seven four five  rochford district matters is edited by  patrick john and produced by rochford  district council who can be found at 3  to 19 south street rochford ss4 1bw  their telephone number is zero one seven  zero two five four six three six six and  their website is at www.rochford.gov  dot uk  the paper is printed by shaman and  company limited  and that brings us to the end of this  edition which was recorded by volunteers  from the rayleigh rochford and castle  point talking newspapers for the blind  at their studio in rochford
 

